      "problem": "${2}^{-9}÷{2}^{-5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n{2}^{-9}÷{2}^{-5}={2}^{(-9)-(-5)}={2}^{-4}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${2}^{-4},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(2)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{2}^{-4}={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{16}\n$$",
